        {
          "unit_id": "first_date",
          "title": "A First Date",
          "description": "Habla de cómo eras y lo que hacías antes con used to. Y would para hábitos repetidos del pasado.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "first_date_lesson",
              "title": "used to",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "A first date",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "You look great. How was Valencia?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Wonderful. I ate too much and slept a lot. My mum still thinks I'm twelve!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Ha! Mine too. When I go home, she makes me eat three dinners."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "So tell me, what were you like as a child?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Oh, I used to be very shy. I didn't use to talk to anyone at school."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "You? Shy? I don't believe it!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "It's true. I used to hide in my room and read books about computers. What about you?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I used to dance flamenco… badly! And I used to want to be a pilot."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "A pilot? Why did you change your mind?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I used to get sick on planes. I still do, actually!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Well, I'm glad you flew to Bristol anyway."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Me too. This is the best restaurant I've been to here."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Then we'll have to come again."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "January, year two. Lucía is back from Valencia with a suntan and a suitcase full of turrón. On Friday night, she meets Daniel at a small Irish restaurant near the harbour."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"I used to be very shy.\" Is Daniel shy now?",
                        "options": [
                          "No, not any more.",
                          "Yes, he still is."
                        ],
                        "answer": 0,
                        "explanation": "Used to habla de algo que era verdad antes y ya no lo es."
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "Which negative is correct?",
                        "options": [
                          "I didn't use to talk to anyone.",
                          "I didn't used to talk to anyone."
                        ],
                        "answer": 0,
                        "explanation": "Después de did / didn't va la forma base: use to."
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "After used to, the verb is…",
                        "options": [
                          "in the base form (be, dance)",
                          "in the -ing form"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "What did Lucía want to be as a child?",
                        "options": [
                          "a pilot",
                          "a dancer",
                          "a designer"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "used to",
                    "explanation": "Used to + verbo en forma base habla de hábitos o situaciones del pasado que ya no son verdad: I used to be very shy (ahora no lo soy).\n\nNegativa: didn't use to (sin -d): I didn't use to talk to anyone. Pregunta: Did you use to dance? — Yes, I did / No, I didn't.\n\nPara una acción que ocurrió una sola vez usamos el past simple: I flew to Bristol in September. Para decir que algo no ha cambiado, still: I still get sick on planes.\n\nNo lo confundas con be used to + -ing (estar acostumbrado a): I'm used to the rain.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Afirmativa",
                          "I used to be very shy."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Negativa",
                          "I didn't use to talk to anyone."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pregunta",
                          "Did you use to dance flamenco?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Respuesta corta",
                          "Yes, I did. / No, I didn't."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Una sola vez (past simple)",
                          "I flew to Bristol in September."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Sigue igual (still)",
                          "I still get sick on planes."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I used to hide in my room and read books about computers.",
                      "I used to want to be a pilot.",
                      "I didn't use to talk to anyone at school.",
                      "I used to get sick on planes. I still do!"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "would for past habits",
                    "explanation": "Para acciones que se repetían en el pasado también se usa would + verbo, sobre todo al contar recuerdos: Every summer we would go to the beach. My mum would make paella on Sundays.\n\nDiferencia con used to:\n• used to sirve para hábitos y para estados: I used to be shy. I used to have long hair.\n• would solo sirve para acciones repetidas, no para estados: no se dice «I would be shy» con ese sentido.\n\nAl contar un recuerdo se suele empezar con used to y seguir con would: When I was a child, I used to spend the summers in Galway. My grandad would take me fishing every morning.\n\nWould se contrae: we'd, she'd.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "used to",
                        "would"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Acción repetida",
                          "We used to go to the beach.",
                          "We would go to the beach."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Estado",
                          "I used to be very shy.",
                          "— (no se usa)"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Posesión",
                          "I used to have a bike.",
                          "— (no se usa)"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Every Sunday my mum would make paella for the whole family.",
                      "Daniel would hide in his room and read about computers.",
                      "I used to be shy. At parties I would sit in a corner and say nothing.",
                      "In summer we'd get up early and go to the beach."
                    ]
                  }
                },
